{
  "schema_version": "3.0",
  "key": "discourse_connectors",
  "concept_slug": "discourse_connectors",
  "grounding_mode": "fallback_no_wiki",
  "title": "Link Ideas with Norwegian Discourse Connectors",
  "cefr_level": "B1",
  "goal": "Use common connectors for sequence, addition, contrast, and conclusion with correct V2 word order.",
  "elements": [
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "orient",
      "title": "What Connectors Do",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Discourse connectors are words and phrases that show how one idea relates to the next. In Norwegian, they help you guide the reader or listener through time, add information, show contrast, or wrap up a point."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "col_langs": [
            "no",
            "en",
            "en"
          ],
          "headers": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "bindeord"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "job"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "basic meaning"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "først"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "sequence"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "first"
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "dessuten"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "addition"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "besides, moreover"
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "likevel"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "contrast against expectation"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "nevertheless, still"
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "derimot"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "contrast between two things"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "on the other hand, however"
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "til slutt"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "conclusion or final step"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "finally, in the end"
                }
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Først leste jeg teksten."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "First I read the text."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Dessuten lærte jeg mange nye ord."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Besides, I learned many new words."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Connector First, Verb Second",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "When a connector starts a main clause, a sentence that can stand alone, it usually fills position 1. Then Norwegian uses V2 word order: the finite verb comes in position 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "If a connector is position 1 in a main clause, put the finite verb immediately after it: connector plus verb plus subject."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Likevel kom hun på møtet."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Still, she came to the meeting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Derimot ville broren hennes bli hjemme."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Her brother, on the other hand, wanted to stay home."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "warning",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Do not add English word order after a fronted connector. Say "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "Likevel kom hun",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": ", not "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "Likevel hun kom",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "contrast",
      "title": "Two Kinds of Contrast",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Norwegian often separates contrast into two useful meanings. Use "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "likevel",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " when the second idea happens despite what you expected. Use "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "derimot",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " when you compare two different people, things, or situations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Det regnet mye. Likevel gikk vi en tur."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "It rained a lot. Nevertheless, we went for a walk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jeg liker kaffe. Søsteren min, derimot, drikker bare te."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I like coffee. My sister, on the other hand, only drinks tea."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Likevel",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " means the result is surprising. "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Derimot",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " marks a comparison or opposite point."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Build a Clear Thread",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "For a short explanation or story, connectors can make the structure visible. Use sequence to start, addition to add a reason, contrast to shift the direction, and a conclusion connector to finish."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Først ryddet vi kjøkkenet. Dessuten vasket vi gulvet. Til slutt laget vi middag."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "First we cleaned the kitchen. Besides, we washed the floor. Finally, we made dinner."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Kurset var dyrt. Likevel meldte jeg meg på. Til slutt var jeg veldig fornøyd."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "The course was expensive. Still, I signed up. In the end, I was very satisfied."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "tip",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Several connectors can appear in the middle of a clause too. This lesson focuses on the common pattern where the connector starts the main clause and triggers V2."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "exercise",
      "id": "ex_categorize_jobs",
      "operation": "categorize",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Sort each connector by its main job."
        }
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Good: each connector signals a different relationship between ideas."
        }
      ],
